# Jolly Challenge — Frontend

Frontend-only React application for the Jolly coding challenge (Show Explorer).
No backend — all logic and state run in the browser.

Product and architecture (requirements, React Query, debounce, races, design
system): [docs/DESIGN_DOC.md](DESIGN_DOC.md).

## Stack

| Layer | Choice |
| ----- | ------ |
| Framework | React 19 + TypeScript |
| Build | Vite |
| Routing | React Router |
| Styling | Tailwind CSS v4 |
| Components | shadcn/ui (Nova, Base UI) — do not recreate primitives |
| Server state | TanStack Query (React Query) |
| Client state | Zustand (favorites persist) |
| Validation | Zod |
| Tests | Vitest + Testing Library; Playwright (E2E in `e2e/`) |

## Folder structure

```
test-fixtures/              # TVMaze mock data (test/e2e only)
  tvmaze.mock-data.ts       # Real API snapshot bundle (spaghetti-exempt)
  tvmaze-mock-handler.ts    # Routes mocked fetch / Playwright responses
e2e/                        # Playwright E2E tests
src/
  app/                   # App shell (providers)
  common/
    components/          # App compositions (app-header, app-bottom-nav, show-status-badge)
    layouts/             # Root layout
    pages/               # Not found
  components/
    ui/                  # shadcn primitives
  lib/
    env.ts               # API_KEY + TVMaze base URL
    query-client.ts      # React Query client (staleTime 1 minute)
    strip-html.ts
    utils.ts             # cn()
  modules/
    shows/               # Browse rows, search grid, filter, hero, infinite scroll
    show-detail/         # Detail hero + episodes by season
    favorites/           # My List (Zustand persist)
  routes/
    index.tsx            # Central route wiring
  styles/
    index.css            # Tailwind v4 + Netflix-inspired tokens
  __tests__/
    setup-storage.ts     # localStorage polyfill (runs first)
    setup.ts             # Vitest setup + global cleanup
    render-app.tsx       # Router + QueryClient test helper
  main.tsx
```

## Design system

Core UI primitives live in `src/components/ui/` and **must not be re-created**
in modules or `src/common/`. Compose them (Button + Input + Select + Badge, etc.).
See [DESIGN_DOC.md](DESIGN_DOC.md) §6.

**Visual language:** Netflix-inspired TV UI — black canvas, Netflix red accent,
cinematic hero, pill CTAs, horizontal poster rows. Tokens in `src/styles/index.css`.

Installed primitives: `button`, `card`, `input`, `select`, `dropdown-menu`,
`badge`, `skeleton`, `separator`, `empty`, `spinner`, `toggle`, `toggle-group`,
`input-group`, `textarea`.

## Module conventions

Each feature module under `src/modules/<name>/` follows the layout in
`.cursor/rules/spaghetti-checker.mdc`:

- `pages/` — one page component per file
- `components/` — one component per file
- `hooks/` — one hook per file
- `schemas/` — Zod schemas (one per file)
- `services/` — API and pure business logic
- `stores/` — Zustand slices (if needed)
- `routes.ts` or `index.ts` — public module surface
- `__tests__/` — all tests (never beside source)

`src/components/ui/` is generated shadcn source (multiple related exports per
file by design). It is exempt from the one-component-per-file rule.

